{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1411253-martial-arts-merit-cost","id":1411253,"title":"Martial Arts Merit Cost","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-08-31T15:04:20-07:00","id":1411253,"title":"Martial Arts Merit Cost","content":"My new group just houserules that the Merit cost for MA makes no sense and that you can take it as an ability right out the gate. They want me to run a game for them and I'm hesitant as I'm new to the system to allow this. It seems that the cost of 4 (which is on par with Artifact 4 or Resources 4) is high enough to significantly affect the balance of the game if we were just to throw it away.<br /> <br /> Is there a good reason the MA merit is so expensive?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3230-tyzerg","name":"Tyzerg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"131"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-31T15:29:45-07:00","id":1411257,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tyzerg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1411253-martial-arts-merit-cost#post1411253\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It seems that the cost of 4 (which is on par with Artifact 4 or Resources 4) is high enough to significantly affect the balance of the game if we were just to throw it away.<br /> <br /> Is there a good reason the MA merit is so expensive?</div> </div> </div> </div>You've hit the nail on the head with the comparison to Artifact 4, I think. If you bought a 4-dot artifact, you could expect to buy evocations for it (up to 15 of them, by the rules in Arms of the Chosen), which significantly improve your character's performance, but are vulnerable to being removed if someone manages to steal the artifact. With Martial Artist, you can buy hypothetically unlimited number of martial arts charms, each style requires you to spend some XP on the Ability for the style, but the charms can be potentially comboed together, and nobody can really take away your ability to be a martial artist. Personally, I think they're reasonably balanced.<br /> <br /> I wasn't part of the playtest for Ex3, but I'm told that what happened, when there <i>wasn't</i> a Martial Artist merit, everybody basically bought martial arts styles. It's basically combat charms that you can spend Solar XP on, which makes it <i>extremely</i> competitive, if not purely better, than the native Solar combat Abilities, if there's no extra buy-in via the merit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-31T15:40:05-07:00","id":1411261,"title":"","content":"While I'm not a particular fan of how all this is implemented RAW:<br /> <br /> Consider the comparison to a 4 dot Daiklave. The value of the Artifact isn't in immediate benefits (you don't get better weapon stat blocks), but a stronger/larger Evocation tree for your weapon. The MA Merit is, effectively the same investment: a bunch of Charms you can buy because of the Merit. While it's difficult to do a direct comparison on a few factors, if you consider MA an Artifact with dozens of Evocations trees instead of one... that's not such a loss.<br /> <br /> Here's a potential compromise (or two) you can pitch if you're worried:<br /> <br /> 1) Instead of having to buy Martial Arts ratings in each style, you buy it once and styles are acquired like Specialties (so closer to Linguistics and Lore). This is, frankly, a much greater XP savings in the long run, but means rushing to master a style at creation is still a significant investment that's harder to combine with Artifact weapon/armor for your style and so on.<br /> <br /> 2) Make the cost of MA variable. Such as at 1 dot you can buy the mundane dots in a MA, but not Charms, at 3 dots you can start buying Charms but you are treated as a Terrestrial for the Terrestrial and Mastery Keywords, and a 4 dots you treat the Keywords as usual. This gives mortal and Dragon-blooded non-Immaculate Monk characters a bit of a break, and allows &quot;dabbling&quot; in MA to be less costly.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-31T15:56:47-07:00","id":1411265,"title":"","content":"From what I understand it's an attempt to balance groups with one martial artist and other players. If you play a solo game, or every player wants martial arts, it makes sense to waive the cost. However, some ST's might think it's stupid and waive the cost anyways.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2783-tytalus","name":"Tytalus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2783_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"491"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-31T16:50:19-07:00","id":1411270,"title":"","content":"My solution to this was that if a character only was buying Charms from a single Martial Art, they didn't need the Merit. As soon as they wanted to buy Charms from more than a single Martial Arts style, then the Merit was required.<br /> <br /> It allows a character that just wants to use a single Martial Art as their combat style flavor of choice the ability to jump right in alongside Melee, Archery, etc. At the same time, it does not let Martial Arts combinations get out of hand without the &quot;system tax&quot; implemented by the designers to curb the run-away martial arts style problem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12111-the_larz","name":"the_larz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-31T17:18:52-07:00","id":1411272,"title":"","content":"I can't really speak to anyone else's experience with the system, but I've run a couple of Solars games waiving the MA merit entirely and haven't noticed any particular imbalance between the players. Maybe, in part, it's that I've never had more than one character particularly interested in being a martial artist in the first place. The core Brawl and Melee charmsets are plenty good on their own. Having to buy up the abilities over and over seems like a significant enough price for some charm access without piling on a 4 point merit. At least the way I run it a good amount of the cost is just finding a teacher and getting them to be willing to teach you, which is usually a bigger hassle than spending 12xp would be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11685-sundance","name":"Sundance","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-31T17:40:48-07:00","id":1411277,"title":"","content":"I don't think doing away with it entirely is the way to go (or people will start 'dabbling' in martial arts which to me doesn't feel right), but it certainly could stand to be 2 dots rather than 4. Yes compared to an artifact it gives you access to a lot more charms you can buy with solar xp but unlike evocations you can't combine them with native solar combat charms (which are generally the best combat charms) and you don't get artifact stats or attunement bonuses. Also there*s only so much solar XP you get over a game, so theoretically being able to buy all those charms is cool and all but few games last long enough that you're sitting around with a bunch of solar xp and nothing to spend it on..<br /> <br /> Given that the 10 merit dots you start with also tend to go to background traits and artifacts that help define your character, having to sink 4 to be a martial artist also feels kinda bad.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2579,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2579-limaxophobiac","user":"limaxophobiac","date":". 08-31-2020, 08:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2579-limaxophobiac","name":"limaxophobiac","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"294"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-31T18:06:15-07:00","id":1411282,"title":"","content":"If you consider the merit cost is necessary to justify access to a handful of powers, you can still drop it to 3, and maybe allow condensing the ability purchases to just one track of dots.<br /> Martial Arts have a very similar role as artifact 3 weapons, and they have to buy each power anyway, so in that sense the expenditure is identical.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-31T19:05:32-07:00","id":1411287,"title":"","content":"The other way you can do it is to remember that Martial Arts technically requires a teacher of some kind. <br /> <br /> You can say that the four merit dots represents <i>them</i>. <br /> <br /> So essentially swap out &quot;martial arts&quot; for a 4 dot mentor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-31T21:57:26-07:00","id":1411299,"title":"","content":"Martial Arts are kinda unique in that (form most styles) They give a grab bag of effects all in one tree. For example Snake style has good damage adders, good soak boosters, good utility gambits, and some movement shenanigans, that is at least 3 abilities worth of stuff that you can grab from only one ability. This is pretty powerful. This is ESPECIALLY powerful when you remember that martial arts can be bought with solar XP instead of regular XP like most charms. If you are going to remove the merit cost I would highly recommend that you not allow purchases with solar XP. If your players want the easy access of all other charms they should have the same restrictions. <br /> <br /> On the other hand I suppose it is more of a relative difference between MA and say melee than a huge power-up in absolute terms, so if all of your players are ok with it then it doesn't really matter that any of them who chose MA will have an advantage over those that don't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9124-satoshi","name":"satoshi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"282"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-01T00:02:15-07:00","id":1411301,"title":"","content":"I think its handled very poorly and the Merit Tax is an answer to a hypothetical problem not a real one. <br /> <br /> There's basically 2 types of MA: I am a primary fighter and I want a unique splash on a noncom. SP and WR a good examples of Primaries. SVN and DPC are the latter. <br /> <br /> Single Point, widely regarded as the most powerful, Surpasses then Ties them Loses to Melee in order of investment. It has arguably the most bang for your buck on a charm-to-power scale but a Dawn SPer is gonna get wrecked by a Melee Dawn. Im too sick to link the Exalted Arena page, but you can find it. <br /> <br /> So SP, the most powerful, is on par with Melee, which doesnt cost anything. You can combo MA charms (I had a great Ebon Shadow Tiger Stylist), but so what? You can already use Thuderbolt Attack Prana without a merit cost and there's no greater combo i can think of in terms of Balance off the top of my head. Just think about Thrown Stealth and Brawl Athletics or Melee Resistance. <br /> <br /> The hammerpoint in this thread so far has been &quot;Solar XP&quot;. So to counter that, do you either A) not let solar xp be spent on MA charms, or B)put a 4 dot merit tax in character creation? <br /> <br /> I don't want to drag EX3 through the mud, but lets not pretend this is a carefully manicured environment. You can get a T-Rex for less than MA. Its <b> One Charm</b> to get a size whatever battlegroup of bloodapes. And its not like Occult is a skill tax since people regularly go for ISoB. Stormcaller is better than most MAs and it cost 5 dots, which is literally cheaper than MAMerit and MASkill 3. Flying Wings/The Nimbus Cloud and a Bow make you literally unkillable for 99% of starting PCs. <br /> <br /> For my own experience, Ebon Shadow + Tiger was a major investment that needed Stealth and the Belt of Shadow Walking to really wow, and honestly Stealth+BoSW+Whatever is probably gonna have the same results for cheaper.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-01T00:59:06-07:00","id":1411305,"title":"","content":"I think that the Martial Artist Merit is overpriced, but I've found that houseruling that the merit lets you pick out 1 martial arts charm for free brings it right back up to the power of a 4-dot Artifact. After all, tons of 4-dots give you an Evocation for free.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11619-kymmetheseventh","name":"KymmetheSeventh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-01T01:49:17-07:00","id":1411310,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1411253-martial-arts-merit-cost?p=1411287#post1411287\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The other way you can do it is to remember that Martial Arts technically requires a teacher of some kind.<br /> <br /> You can say that the four merit dots represents <i>them</i>.<br /> <br /> So essentially swap out &amp;quot;martial arts&amp;quot; for a 4 dot mentor.</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019m all for the MA merit also representing one story merit say, Mentor 3, or Ally 3 (basically a story merit one dot lower) for immersion purposes.<br /> <br /> (Mentor 3 can be the all knowing Sensei, Ally 3 could be the Shonen anime protag who teaches you their finishing move because they are such a bro, leading to you inevitably exceeding them in skill and ability).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8959,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","user":"prototype00","date":". 09-01-2020, 06:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-01T05:15:22-07:00","id":1411328,"title":"","content":"On my end we ditched it almost completely. You can buy the abilities directly (and the relevant techniques through them) or buy the merit and use brawl for everything.<br /> Nothing breaks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-01T12:52:13-07:00","id":1411417,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KymmetheSeventh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1411253-martial-arts-merit-cost?p=1411305#post1411305\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that the Martial Artist Merit is overpriced, but I've found that houseruling that the merit lets you pick out 1 martial arts charm for free brings it right back up to the power of a 4-dot Artifact. After all, tons of 4-dots give you an Evocation for free.</div> </div> </div> </div>This I like. See also: Divine Heritage coming with your first such Eclipse Charm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-03T13:00:42-07:00","id":1411681,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1411253-martial-arts-merit-cost?p=1411301#post1411301\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think its handled very poorly and the Merit Tax is an answer to a hypothetical problem not a real one.<br /> <br /> There's basically 2 types of MA: I am a primary fighter and I want a unique splash on a noncom. SP and WR a good examples of Primaries. SVN and DPC are the latter.<br /> <br /> Single Point, widely regarded as the most powerful, Surpasses then Ties them Loses to Melee in order of investment. It has arguably the most bang for your buck on a charm-to-power scale but a Dawn SPer is gonna get wrecked by a Melee Dawn. Im too sick to link the Exalted Arena page, but you can find it.</div> </div> </div> </div>This doesn't matter much when a Melee Supernal Dawn is the <i>least likely possible</i> non-mortal opponent a Dawn is going to face. Nothing in the games implies that Solars come to blows very often in the second age (for instance the 3e core book provides no quick and dirty templates for making Solar opponents--though it does for other Exalted). The vast majority of supernatural opponents a Dawn with SPSitV will face are:<br /> <br /> -Dragon-blooded/Liminals<br /> -Gods/Elementals<br /> -Maybe an Abyssal<br /> <br /> All of which besides the possibly the Abyssal (and only if they are a Dusk with whatever the Abyssal equivalent of Supernal Melee is) will get absolutely blown to smithereens by a Mastery-enhanced Single Point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4801-frostav","name":"Frostav","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-03T14:35:15-07:00","id":1411704,"title":"","content":"Before this gets too far, can we all agree on a simple issue?<br /> <br /> The Martial Arts Merit <b>isn't fun</b>. For all we can argue about the value and if it even has any, MA vs Melee, the Merit vs. an Artifact, or whatever... the RAW Merit is a point/XP tax before you can spend more points/XP that actually do something. Even if you never buy any Evocations, an Artifact weapon is still a kickass weapon, and is thus fun to have. Melee 5, even if you never take any Melee Charms, still makes you one of the best human hand-to-hand weapon combatants in Creation and presumably you have some other tricks up your sleeve.<br /> <br /> Even talking about the point cost itself is fairly meaningless because the Merit costs are all over the place. They only way to make any sense of price for impact and story/innate/purchased is to presume a very specific mindset about what kind of rolls are more important than others. Fleet of Foot costs four points as well, and it's still just a +1 die to some Athletics rolls.<br /> <br /> The MA Merit, by itself, is just there to sink points into.<br /> <br /> Even if you agree with the logic that MA needs some gating, this is a poor way to do it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-04T04:45:10-07:00","id":1411771,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Frostav</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1411253-martial-arts-merit-cost?p=1411681#post1411681\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This doesn't matter much when a Melee Supernal Dawn is the <i>least likely possible</i> non-mortal opponent a Dawn is going to face. Nothing in the games implies that Solars come to blows very often in the second age (for instance the 3e core book provides no quick and dirty templates for making Solar opponents--though it does for other Exalted). The vast majority of supernatural opponents a Dawn with SPSitV will face are:<br /> <br /> -Dragon-blooded/Liminals<br /> -Gods/Elementals<br /> -Maybe an Abyssal<br /> <br /> All of which besides the possibly the Abyssal (and only if they are a Dusk with whatever the Abyssal equivalent of Supernal Melee is) will get absolutely blown to smithereens by a Mastery-enhanced Single Point.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree. You thoroughly refuted an argument I didn't make though. SP isnt as strong as Melee, but it has a Merit Tax is the point. And as HeavyArms said, its just not *fun* to pay a merit tax, its bad game design. <br /> <br /> You buy a 4 dot artifact and you dont just get evocations, you get a totally bomb ass sword out of the deal. Nothing justifies the MA merit and you dont get crackerjack toy with it. <br /> <br /> And also, if you arent a dawn then the powerful charms arent available at chargen, and depending on your group its 5ish sessions before you hit E2 and you even unlock form charms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-04T04:52:30-07:00","id":1411772,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1411253-martial-arts-merit-cost?p=1411771#post1411771\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I agree. You thoroughly refuted an argument I didn't make though. SP isnt as strong as Melee, but it has a Merit Tax is the point. And as HeavyArms said, its just not *fun* to pay a merit tax, its bad game design.<br /> <br /> You buy a 4 dot artifact and you dont just get evocations, you get a totally bomb ass sword out of the deal. Nothing justifies the MA merit and you dont get crackerjack toy with it.<br /> <br /> And also, if you arent a dawn then the powerful charms arent available at chargen, and depending on your group its 5ish sessions before you hit E2 and you even unlock form charms.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think supposedly Martial Arts is supposed to come with some other stuff (access to private MA tournaments where you can talk secrets organizations, access to gods/old hermits than only speak to those who have mastered the ultimate Snake Strike, etc ...) but the game does not support this enough in its description, so it's effectively useless as anything else that a combat ability.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-04T13:35:32-07:00","id":1411870,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1411253-martial-arts-merit-cost?p=1411771#post1411771\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">SP isnt as strong as Melee, but it has a Merit Tax is the point. And as HeavyArms said, its just not *fun* to pay a merit tax, its bad game design.</div> </div> </div> </div>Since you're invoking me a bit here...<br /> <br /> It's worth going back to post #2 and Kelly's point about Solar XP vs.normal XP.<br /> <br /> One of the things about MA is that it's really good if you're not a Dawn and you want some potent combat utility: you don't have to give up spending on your primary focus Charms to buy up your MA Charms too. If you're making an Eclipse social butterfly, the dual XP tracks makes MA a much stronger contender than native Solar Charms that would impede your progress in places like Presence and Socialize. It also has the benefit of, as long as you're careful about your Anima, not giving you away as easily.<br /> <br /> Stuff that doesn't always come out as well in things like The Arena.<br /> <br /> Of course, I still think the RAW way to having players weigh this is dumb, but I can't deny that if you're not a combat primary character without some gating MA is pretty much a must have in Exalted as such a default combat-heavy game. The amount of XP in the RAW you have to sink in MA is enough to question if that's really where you want to invest your non-native Charm XP.<br /> <br /> Now, for a lot of groups? I don't think they actually have a problem with this: hence so many drop the gating completely. Of course your social butterfly Eclipse grabs SVN or DPC... that's what those MAs are for, and you're not going to outshine a dedicated Dawn Melee fighter in the long run. Though in 2e that's how we ended up with the Dawn Solution. It's also not exactly fun for the Dawn players where they're &quot;shtick&quot; is being slightly better at combat because they have their kick ass Solar Charms, while everyone else gets cool evocative fighting styles that help match their character concepts. It's not great game design to have player be forced to pick between optimal but boring, and less than optimal but cool.<br /> <br /> So it's probably best to focus our energy in a different place: How do we make this all equally fun to play?<br /> <br /> If we take the playtest reports at face value and that MA needs some gating, is there a better method besides the Merit tax?<br /> <br /> If we need to at least keep the Merit for gating, what can we do to make the Merit more fun and less tax? What crackerjacks would you add that don't make it too good in the process?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1411253-martial-arts-merit-cost?p=1411772#post1411772\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think supposedly Martial Arts is supposed to come with some other stuff (access to private MA tournaments where you can talk secrets organizations, access to gods/old hermits than only speak to those who have mastered the ultimate Snake Strike, etc ...) but the game does not support this enough in its description, so it's effectively useless as anything else that a combat ability.</div> </div> </div> </div>There were a lot of things that MA was supposed to do... we'll see if any of that ever comes to fruition fr 3e. Once upon a time mundane MA styles were supposed to work kind of like Fighting Style Merits from the CofD (thus giving the MA Merit value even for mortals), but that got dropped as the devs couldn't balance it with Charms or some such.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-04T13:40:50-07:00","id":1411873,"title":"","content":"I felt the earlier suggestion of giving a free MA Charm or two with the initial purchase of the Merit is fun but not overpowering, putting it on par with the kinds of artifacts that grant you a free Evocation when you first attune to it.<br /> <br /> \u200b(I don't personally have a problem with the Merit but I feel for the people who do, hence why I'm chiming in, as I feel it's a pretty decent compromise.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-04T14:46:56-07:00","id":1411895,"title":"","content":"The biggest problem with the free Charm is you have to qualify for the Charm in the first place (which yes, isn't hard and would be weird not to do). It's not a hard fix (XP debt for anything your lacking) but it's a consideration.<br /> <br /> Though it doesn't do anything for mortals that take MA.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-04T15:22:21-07:00","id":1411905,"title":"","content":"Mortals aren't really a point of consideration here. This isn't about them in any meaningful way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-04T15:48:10-07:00","id":1411915,"title":"","content":"This is a thread about whether or not the cost/benefit of the Martial Arts Merit are warranted; and possibly what to do if you don't think they are.<br /> <br /> As:<br /> <br /> 1) The book contains rules for playing mortals either as their own thing or to do pre-Exaltation play.<br /> <br /> 2) The MA Merit applies to PC mortals, or if for some reason a NPC is stated up as a full character it would apply to them too.<br /> <br /> Then mortals are a point of consideration here. Whether or not you care doesn't mean the rest of us feel the same way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-05T04:17:24-07:00","id":1412047,"title":"","content":"I also like the suggestion of the free charm.<br /> Additionally, I'd seriously consider the cost of the merit for a Dawn Caste who took Martial Arts as their Supernal ability since under those circumstances it's in direct competition with the likes of Solar Melee and many of the benefits of being able to treat a Martial Art like it's an Evocation tree would be lost.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-05T16:10:56-07:00","id":1412178,"title":"","content":"Supernal MA is a weird thing with how everything is structured. Really, the only reason to do it is to start with a full MA style mastered or close to it. If you're planning on mastering 3-4 styles or something, it doesn't really help in that situation.<br /> <br /> Sure, all Supernals run into that as your Essence increases, but most of the Abilities have more side Charms, branches, and you can theoretically design custom Charms, which means you'll still have plenty of Charms over your Essence to grab for a good deal of play.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-05T17:49:46-07:00","id":1412190,"title":"","content":"The Merit wouldn't bother me except... you also need separate Ability dots.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-05T18:33:18-07:00","id":1412196,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1411253-martial-arts-merit-cost?p=1412178#post1412178\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Supernal MA is a weird thing with how everything is structured. Really, the only reason to do it is to start with a full MA style mastered or close to it. If you're planning on mastering 3-4 styles or something, it doesn't really help in that situation.<br /> <br /> Sure, all Supernals run into that as your Essence increases, but most of the Abilities have more side Charms, branches, and you can theoretically design custom Charms, which means you'll still have plenty of Charms over your Essence to grab for a good deal of play.</div> </div> </div> </div>I had a player who did this in our separate mini campaign we ran when some players werent around for the main campaign. He made a Dawn Snake master and... yeah that was it. There was no way to get better at Snake than he was at CharGen. He picked up some Dodge and some non-com stuff like Lore and Investigate, but fundamentally he couldn't get better at actually being a Snake Stylist than he was at session 1, which is a really, <i>really</i> weird thing to think about in a game so heavily inspired by Wuxia.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-05T20:17:33-07:00","id":1412212,"title":"","content":"As far as the Wuxia inspirations... that's not really a problem. Frequently &quot;master of X style&quot; means they're going to grow in other areas.<br /> <br /> One of the larger problems is that MA isn't really built to compliment each other. Like, one beat that's really missing from Wuxia is masters of multiple styles swapping styles out to try to outmaneuver each other. Sure, if it's one-on-one and both take the Simple action to swap forms that can work, but it doesn't really do that in action in regular Exalted play. There also isn't really an eye towards making sure that the MA styles that get made all have strong niches that a multi-stylist is going to want to swap styles to match the situation.<br /> <br /> This is pretty far from the Merit itself, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-06T02:15:48-07:00","id":1412236,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1411253-martial-arts-merit-cost?p=1412212#post1412212\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of the larger problems is that MA isn't really built to compliment each other. Like, one beat that's really missing from Wuxia is masters of multiple styles swapping styles out to try to outmaneuver each other. Sure, if it's one-on-one and both take the Simple action to swap forms that can work, but it doesn't really do that in action in regular Exalted play.</div> </div> </div> </div>Often Wuxia is about demonstrating the superiority of the protagonist's signature style (&quot;Japanese karate is no match for my kung fu!&quot;)<br /> <br /> But I'm reminded of this KSBD arc: <a href=\"https://killsixbilliondemons.com/comic/king-of-swords-10-147/\" target=\"_blank\">https://killsixbilliondemons.com/com...swords-10-147/</a><br /> <a href=\"https://killsixbilliondemons.com/comic/king-of-swords-10-149/\" target=\"_blank\">https://killsixbilliondemons.com/com...swords-10-149/</a><br /> <a href=\"https://killsixbilliondemons.com/comic/king-of-swords-10-158/\" target=\"_blank\">https://killsixbilliondemons.com/com...swords-10-158/</a><br /> <br /> I think the Reflexive Form activation conditions handle swapping styles really well... but I hope Sids will have a way of mixing styles more effectively.<br /> <br /> But each MA has a pretty strong theme. If you're fighting someone in heavy armor, you can switch to Snake, if you're fighting a Smash fighter you can switch to Tiger, White Reaper for battlegroups, etc..","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-06T09:32:15-07:00","id":1412300,"title":"","content":"Mortal martial artists, meaning &quot;people who can perform Martial Arts Charms,&quot; do not and cannot exist in the current edition of Exalted. Period. Therefore, &quot;Martial Artist&quot; is a Merit of no value for mortals. Mortal practitioners of the forms of various styles can and do exist, but do not and cannot have Charms; in mechanical terms, they have specialties and stunt like crazy.Thus, the Martial Artist merit, the sole purpose of which is to grant access to Martial Arts Charms, is of no value whatsoever to mortals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-06T09:32:45-07:00","id":1412301,"title":"","content":"Multipost.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1184,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","user":"LadyLens","date":". 09-06-2020, 10:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-06T09:33:35-07:00","id":1412302,"title":"","content":"Multipost.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1184,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","user":"LadyLens","date":". 09-06-2020, 10:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-06T09:34:17-07:00","id":1412303,"title":"","content":"Multipost.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1184,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","user":"LadyLens","date":". 09-06-2020, 10:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-06T09:35:06-07:00","id":1412304,"title":"","content":"Multipost.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1184,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","user":"LadyLens","date":". 09-06-2020, 10:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-06T14:38:54-07:00","id":1412332,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1411253-martial-arts-merit-cost?p=1412236#post1412236\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Often Wuxia is about demonstrating the superiority of the protagonist's signature style (&quot;Japanese karate is no match for my kung fu!&quot;)</div> </div> </div> </div>Not.. really? While &quot;dojo rivalries&quot; are certainly part of Wuxia, Wuxia generally focuses on that to set up a villain's motivations (&quot;Our sifu wouldn't teach me the ultimate secrets of his kung fu, but I found a new sifu...&quot;) than the straight up style-offs of modern martial arts action movies.<br /> <br /> Wuxia wouldn't have genre tropes around the heroes earning permission to learn from new masters to expand their training if it wasn't something the genre supported happening: it's more about those who do it with respect and humility vs. those that do it for lesser reasons. Wuxia is about the triumph of heroes because living well is more powerful than mastering techniques, more than it is about proving which styles are superior.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think the Reflexive Form activation conditions handle swapping styles really well... </div> </div> </div>I think they're a good start, but it's hard to flow as naturally as it could. Some styles can swap easily (Snake and Tiger for example are great for that), while SP can only be reflexive at the start of a fight so you can never swap back to it if you swap to something else.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LadyLens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1411253-martial-arts-merit-cost?p=1412304#post1412304\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mortal martial artists, meaning &quot;people who can perform Martial Arts Charms,&quot; do not and cannot exist in the current edition of Exalted. Period.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mortals, however, still need the Merit to buy dots in Martial Arts as an Ability.<br /> <br /> If I want to make a mortal that uses hook swords, RAW, I have to take Brawl 1, the Martial Arts Merit, and at least one dot in Martial Arts (Snake Style) or some other hook sword using style. Taking Melee 1 with a specialty in Hook Swords or Snake Style doesn't work.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Therefore, &quot;Martial Artist&quot; is a Merit of no value for mortals. </div> </div> </div>It isn't of no value, it's just of shitty value. More importantly, the value set is completely at odds with how the setting is supposed to work. There are supposed to be lots of mortals running around creation that have studied martial arts that explicitly use the Martial Arts dots that are the dots needed to buy MA Charms. The only way for them to get those dots is to go through the MA Merit even if they never get to buy Charms as the Merit is priced around.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Mortal practitioners of the forms of various styles can and do exist, but do not and cannot have Charms; in mechanical terms, they have specialties and stunt like crazy. </div> </div> </div>Citation needed. According to the Martial Arts Tag in the weapons section, you need dots in a relevant Martial Art to use those weapons, and the only way to buy those Martial Arts dots is if you have the Merit.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Thus, the Martial Artist merit, the sole purpose of which is to grant access to Martial Arts Charms, is of no value whatsoever to mortals. </div> </div> </div>Again, the MA Merit's sole purpose is to let you buy dots in MA Abilities, which are then prerequisites to MA Charms. If you want to use MA Abilities without the Charms, you still need the Merit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-06T15:13:22-07:00","id":1412335,"title":"","content":"New question:<br /> <br /> Do you generally want a new Martial Arts Charm, or to start play with multiple Martial Charms because<br /> <br /> 1) You want to be stronger?<br /> <br /> or<br /> <br /> 2) You want enough interesting options to choose from in battle? Not necessarily in the sense that you'll be more powerful through greater versatility, but in the sense that you won't be left in a situation where you don't have an interesting action to take, or so that you can choose to do something different when you might otherwise be stuck doing the same thing over and over again until it grows stale.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-06T15:36:42-07:00","id":1412338,"title":"","content":"To answer this new question, I'm only interested in Martial Arts that let me do things native charm sets can't do, or it fits a character theme and so I took it for rp. <br /> <br /> My ES/Tiger Night yakuza had a shadow assassin thing going on. <br /> <br /> My (ST NPC) Lunar Witch of the Swamps used Snake to match her creepy poisons, voodoo, and black magic vibe. <br /> <br /> When I wanted to make a badass Dawn wandering swordsman, I used Melee.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-06T16:17:31-07:00","id":1412342,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure the question can be answered directly, esp. as there's other options.<br /> <br /> Frankly, if I'm looking at making a character that's going to invest in MA, I want all of the following, in no particular order and in variable levels of focus depending on the character and game:<br /> <br /> - Yes, to be more powerful, even if through versatility over raw power. I don't like it when games make you pay XP/creation points just to add flair. Buying Charms is about making a character more powerful on a fundamental design level.<br /> <br /> - Yes, the appeal of MA is increasing your options in combat, letting you have more options than &quot;I hit better/harder.&quot; That's part of the appeal of MA in that they frequently cross into things like Stealth, Athletics, Resistance, and so on: you get a lot more things out of one investment instead of having to branch out into lots of different Abilities.<br /> <br /> - Another appeal of MA is built in combat approaches. MAs can be fun because they're really good in some situations and really bad in other, letting you be really awesome without the lack of weaknesses expanding your native Charms does.<br /> <br /> - Another appeal is flavor outside your native Charms. This doesn't invalidate my first listed point, but as noted above, making a character with a specific theme is frequently better supported in combat by MA than general charms .","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-06T16:24:42-07:00","id":1412344,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LadyLens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1411253-martial-arts-merit-cost?p=1412300#post1412300\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mortal martial artists, meaning &quot;people who can perform Martial Arts Charms,&quot; do not and cannot exist in the current edition of Exalted. Period.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, if you're going to define some thing by establishing it as a contradiction in terms, then the thing cannot exist.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-06T22:19:06-07:00","id":1412394,"title":"","content":"Mortals can't do Exalted Martial Arts unless they literally <i>reach enlightenment</i> first to get a mote pool. Otherwise they buy the merit just to punch things in a funny way or use a wonky sword.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-06T23:48:55-07:00","id":1412401,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1411253-martial-arts-merit-cost?p=1412332#post1412332\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think they're a good start, but it's hard to flow as naturally as it could. Some styles can swap easily (Snake and Tiger for example are great for that), while SP can only be reflexive at the start of a fight so you can never swap back to it if you swap to something else.</div> </div> </div> </div>Single Point can also only be practised with a single weapon and can't be used unarmed. It's the definitive sword style, focusing on drawing your weapon for a killing blow. It's really not meant to be combo'd.<br /> <br /> It's the Iaido style you open with with a mind to finish with, falling back on other styles if you are disarmed etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 09-07-2020, 04:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-07T03:58:44-07:00","id":1412408,"title":"","content":"And? The point wasn't, &quot;SP's special activation doesn't make sense,&quot; but that the special activation rules aren't designed to emulate martial arts masters switching styles to match their opponents' changed tactics as seen in many Wuxia and martial arts fiction that's inspiration for Exalted.<br /> <br /> Styles where switching between them in combat is actually practical is incidental, not purposeful.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-07T05:04:11-07:00","id":1412412,"title":"","content":"But absolutely nothing stops you from using Armor-Penetrating Fang Strike instead of Elegant Weapon Repertoire if you want to switch up your style mid-fight, at-will.<br /> <br /> You choose which of your martial arts techniques to use on each attack. You can change styles every single round.<br /> <br /> So... sure, the Form Special Activations don't do that. Step One of Attack Resolution does that.<br /> <br /> The Form Charms give you additional bonuses for fighting in a particular style, and have Special Activation rules to let you Reflexively use them when you do something iconic to that method of fighting.<br /> <br /> If I want to switch from Tiger to Snake, all I need to do is Stunt differently. But the Reflexive activation of Snake Form really helps me <i>gain an advantage</i> by switching styles.<br /> <br /> In real life, I can switch from boxing to karate whenever I want. But just switching doesn't give me an advantage -- the circumstances have to be right. Karate and boxing weren't invented to syngerise with each other. Though I'm sure there are plenty of MMA fighters who have worked elements of each into their fighting styles. Exalted's Martial Arts should be written as complete, distinct styles -- it's the player's job to work out synergy and combos.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-07T08:26:12-07:00","id":1412437,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1411253-martial-arts-merit-cost?p=1412332#post1412332\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It isn't of no value, it's just of shitty value.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed. Access to three extra weapons is not worth 4 merit point. I wouldn't charge any merit points.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1411253-martial-arts-merit-cost?p=1412332#post1412332\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are supposed to be lots of mortals running around creation that have studied martial arts that explicitly use the Martial Arts dots that are the dots needed to buy MA Charms.</div> </div> </div> </div>That does need a citation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-07T08:35:15-07:00","id":1412439,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LadyLens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1411253-martial-arts-merit-cost?p=1412437#post1412437\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That does need a citation.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm reading The Realm and the book empathize the presence of many monks and students of martial arts across the Blessed Isle at least. I don't have the book atm but I think his point is fair.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-07T10:19:57-07:00","id":1412447,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1411253-martial-arts-merit-cost?p=1412412#post1412412\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But absolutely nothing stops you from using Armor-Penetrating Fang Strike instead of Elegant Weapon Repertoire if you want to switch up your style mid-fight, at-will.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is there a particular place you're going with all this? It feels like you're trying to find some sort of perfect nitpick that will somehow unravel my view on this... or at least are just debating minutiae with no actual care for what original point was being made.<br /> <br /> My contention is that the way Exalted handles Martial Arts Charms poorly represents the genre it's primarily drawing from for inspiration around martial arts in the setting. The fact that it's easy to pick and choose MA Charms from different styles (outside of Forms) at will only emphasizes that issue. While blending styles should be a thing because Exalted's inspirations are many and some do that too, the majority of its inspirations treat martial arts styles as more holistic endeavors.... which is why there are tropes around masters facing off with mental chess games as they adopt different forms in response to each other before they actually commit to action. They don't just pick and choose the best moves from all their styles.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> it's the player's job to work out synergy and combos. </div> </div> </div>Why? While some groups might enjoy char-op and such, it's not an inherent job of players to solve puzzles the designers left in the system instead of explaining. You're certainly not going to successfully sell me on the idea that Exalted works better as a game when it makes the mechanics harder for the players to utilize fully by artificially increasing the amount of system mastery needed to do so.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LadyLens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1411253-martial-arts-merit-cost?p=1412437#post1412437\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wouldn't charge any merit points.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fine, but that's explicitly house ruling the game. Please stop trying to make it sound like it isn't.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That does need a citation. </div> </div> </div>3e Core, p. 28 and The Realm p. 97 both state that all Immaculate monks (not just Exalted ones) study martial arts. The Realm is even more explicit in stating that all monks learn one of the five Dragon Styles to the point of mastering both the unarmed and armed basics of that style, just to reach the First Coil and actually be assigned to any duties within the Order. Every Immaculate monk across creation receives training in something that requires the Martial Arts Merit to achieve mechanically.<br /> <br /> 3e Core, p. 163 specifies that the MA Merit represents &quot;systemic training&quot; from somewhere like the Immaculate Order or dojos.<br /> <br /> 3e Core, p. 230 says martial arts tournaments are a thing in Creation.<br /> <br /> 3e Core, p. 426 this is probably the big one, so I'll quote: &quot;Creation\u2019s martial arts are the stuff of legend, powerful fighting styles that emulate the ferocity of mighty beasts or follow paths of esoteric wisdom. Martial artists come in many forms throughout the world. The vast majority are mortal men and women who\u2019ve attained extraordinary martial prowess through intense study, discipline, and training.&quot; I'll also just note once here that throughout the MA section of Chapter 7, there is a stress on there being numerous students and sifus of most styles, leading to the strong impression that it's not just the Exalted doing all this.<br /> <br /> 3e Core, p. 427 says that Snake style is flourishing in the dojos of the South and the East and is seen across Creation.<br /> <br /> 3e Core, p. 447 notes that most dojos across Creation only know Silver-Voiced Nightingale Style as Nightingale Style.<br /> <br /> The Realm, p. 137 notes that Silent Thunder Prefecture has a history of martial arts from when an Immaculate taught the peasants to aid them against the Empress.<br /> <br /> The Realm, p. 172 talks about the Thirteen Schools of Wu-Jian, which are underground martial arts societies.<br /> <br /> DB 3e, p. 65 says that House Sesus has a secret location in the Skyhewn Mountains for teaching &quot;devious schools&quot; of martial arts.<br /> <br /> DB 3e, p. 301 mentions the multitude of groups that practice Golden Janissary Style.<br /> <br /> DB 3e, p. 303 Mantis Style is also very popular in the East and South apparently (makes you wonder about the West and North getting some love with popular MA styles in those areas), as well as commonly studied by the Immaculate monks.<br /> <br /> DB 3e, p. 305 There is nothing here.<br /> <br /> Lunars 3e, p. 67 Skandhar-Bhal is a whole settlement to support the Order of the Moon-That-Fell with it's own warrior monks.<br /> <br /> Lunars 3e. p. 298 Centipede Style is... popular in the East and South (see?) but also the West! Such much so that there are Snake vs. Centipede rivalries in some places, and dojos that mix the two in others.<br /> <br /> Lunars 3e, p. 300 Falcon style is common in the South and had multiple masters spread it to all the other directions.<br /> <br /> Lunars 3e, p. 303 Laughing Monster Style has, &quot;spread to numerous dojos, secret societies, and criminal syndicates.&quot; <br /> <br /> Lunars 3e. p. 306 Swaying Grass Dance Style is, in honor of its origins, secretly taught to slaves and rebels to increase their chances against their oppressors.<br /> <br /> Hopefully that's sufficient to make my point about how the setting is presented.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-07T11:09:18-07:00","id":1412452,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1411253-martial-arts-merit-cost?p=1412447#post1412447\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there a particular place you're going with all this? It feels like you're trying to find some sort of perfect nitpick that will somehow unravel my view on this... or at least are just debating minutiae with no actual care for what original point was being made.</div> </div> </div> </div>My point is simple: Exalted Martial Arts are not Burn Legend. It's not meant to be Wuxia The RPG. But it is inspired by Wuxia and is perfectly sufficient for playing a Wuxia inspired character in the fictional world of Creation &quot;as is&quot;.<br /> <br /> You want to have one style? You can do that. You want a wise old master? You can have that. You want to travel the world learning new styles? Go right ahead. You want to use the right style for the right situation to gain an advantage? That's exactly how the system works RAW. You want to mix styles? You can.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying your complaint is baseless. You've got a valid point. If you and four friends want to act out a Wuxia film, then Exalted is a very poor system for that. Very poor. But if you want to play a game about the Chosen of the Gods and one of your friends wants to be a kung fu master and another wants to be a flamethrower specialist then Exalted works quite well.<br /> <br /> I'm not trying to &quot;nitpick&quot;, I'm trying to get you to consider the way Exalted does work and how it can express the themes you want to explore.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> My contention is that the way Exalted handles Martial Arts Charms poorly represents the genre it's primarily drawing from for inspiration around martial arts in the setting. The fact that it's easy to pick and choose MA Charms from different styles (outside of Forms) at will only emphasizes that issue. While blending styles should be a thing because Exalted's inspirations are many and some do that too, the majority of its inspirations treat martial arts styles as more holistic endeavors.... which is why there are tropes around masters facing off with mental chess games as they adopt different forms in response to each other before they actually commit to action. They don't just pick and choose the best moves from all their styles. </div> </div> </div>I don't think the level of granularity you are shooting for is desirable in Exalted. But I don't want to argue with you so... I'd say &quot;agree to disagree&quot;... only I agree with you: don't use Exalted if you want to play a Wuxia RPG. Exalted is a mythic fantasy RPG that draws on Wuxia as an inspiration.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Why? While some groups might enjoy char-op and such, it's not an inherent job of players to solve puzzles the designers left in the system instead of explaining. You're certainly not going to successfully sell me on the idea that Exalted works better as a game when it makes the mechanics harder for the players to utilize fully by artificially increasing the amount of system mastery needed to do so.But </div> </div> </div>That's the game.<br /> <br /> I want styles to be holistic endeavours. I don't want a system built around me having to take Water Dragon Charms to make my Tiger Stylist work. If I'm playing a Tiger Stylist, I want Tiger Style to be a whole and complete Martial Art that gives me a distinct fighting style.<br /> <br /> I don't want the Devs telling me how to make my character. I want them to give me the tools I need to make the character I want to make.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 09-07-2020, 02:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-07T11:26:10-07:00","id":1412453,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1411253-martial-arts-merit-cost?p=1412447#post1412447\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hopefully that's sufficient to make my point about how the setting is presented.</div> </div> </div> </div> Well played. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-07T12:21:00-07:00","id":1412461,"title":"","content":"I don't want to talk for Lady Lens, but I seriously doubt that every NPC martial artist has the Martial Artist Merit. I'd say the vast majority are trivial characters without a statline. Of those with stats, the vast majority are QCs who won't even have a dicepool for &quot;Snake Style 5 dice&quot;: they'll have &quot;Punch Accuracy 8 Damage 8&quot;. Of the tiny percentage that aren't QCs, the NPCs don't have any limit on how many Merit dots they can have so Martial Artist being a four dot Merit is kinda meaningless.<br /> <br /> Just look at the QCs with Charms. They don't have all the prerequisite Charms that PCs need. But, frankly, it's so incidental to the conversation I'm just going to say &quot;meh&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-07T13:51:58-07:00","id":1412476,"title":"","content":"Having reread the quotation, I see it meant something other than what I thought originally.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-07T15:17:16-07:00","id":1412484,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1411253-martial-arts-merit-cost?p=1412452#post1412452\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My point is simple: Exalted Martial Arts are not Burn Legend. It's not meant to be Wuxia The RPG. But it is inspired by Wuxia and is perfectly sufficient for playing a Wuxia inspired character in the fictional world of Creation &quot;as is&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Your point is misplaced... this whole tangent is based on my response to someone else bringing up the Wuxia inspirations for Exalted.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If you and four friends want to act out a Wuxia film, then Exalted is a very poor system for that. </div> </div> </div>Actually, it's a fairly functional system for it... even if 2e is probably easier for executing the concept by having Enlightened Mortals as a thing. Most of what Wuxia does is very Exalted because Wuxia isn't just about martial arts battles.<br /> <br /> I'm... very curious to hear your definition of Wuxia at this point because it feels like we're talking about two different things. Burn Legend isn't Wuxia in the slightest.<br /> <br /> The Bride with White Hair is Wuxia and while not a great plot for a game with a bunch of friends is extremely easy to set in Creation. Here:<br /> <br /> A Dragon-Blooded that was trained by the Immaculate Order but didn't take his vows is working as part of the Wild Hunt. His team is sent out on a mission to destroy an Anathema cult. While investigating, he encounters a strange woman, and the two fall in love. It turns out she's the adopted daughter of the Anathema, but agrees to flee her parental figure to be with her lover; saving her as the cult is destroyed. After spending some time together, the Terrestrial returns to his fellow hunters only to find them all slaughtered and his lover blamed as the only remaining member of the cult so she clearly did it for revenge. Choosing duty over love, he proceeds to chase her down, with some fresh reinforcements, however enraged at his betrayal she reveals she's a Lunar and starts whooping ass to protect herself from the false accusations. As the former lovers square off, the Akuma that was leading the cult reveals it's not dead, and had framed the Lunar, and smack talks them for being so easily manipulated. The two team up and finish the Akuma off for real. The Lunar then flips off the Dragon-blooded for being an ass and goes off into the wilderness.<br /> <br /> Why, exactly, is Exalted a bad game for that sort of genre story? What isn't Exalted going to do (besides adjusting for what's more of a single player game instead of a group one) to support that?<br /> <br /> The only core problem with most Wuxia and Exalted is the same problem with most sources of inspiration and RPGs: most stories focus on a single protagonist.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But if you want to play a game about the Chosen of the Gods and one of your friends wants to be a kung fu master and another wants to be a flamethrower specialist then Exalted works quite well. </div> </div> </div>Except... this whole thread is about how that's not exactly the case because Exalted puts martial arts in a weird place mechanically. Even at a minimum the 1 Ability dot and 4 Merit dot tax that the kung fu master has to deal with that the firewand specialist can just skill by going Archery makes this less true than it should be.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm not trying to &quot;nitpick&quot;, </div> </div> </div>But it's all you're really doing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm trying to get you to consider the way Exalted does work and how it can express the themes you want to explore. </div> </div> </div>I've been playing Exalted for 19 years. I know how it works, and I know how well it does certain things. I don't need you to &quot;get me to consider&quot; anything, and I didn't ask for you opinion or advice on a specific thing for such feedback in this thread.<br /> <br /> I've mildly mused that Exalted moving MA closer to its Wuxia roots might actually be for the better, maybe you should consider what that really means rather than dismiss it out of hand.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don't think the level of granularity you are shooting for is desirable in Exalted. </div> </div> </div>I haven't expressed any level of granularity preference in this matter. I've said that there's tropes that are oddly not present in Exalted given its inspirations.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But I don't want to argue with you so... I'd say &quot;agree to disagree&quot;... only I agree with you: don't use Exalted if you want to play a Wuxia RPG. Exalted is a mythic fantasy RPG that draws on Wuxia as an inspiration. </div> </div> </div>That's not agreeing with me. That's putting words in my mouth.<br /> <br /> You do realize the Wuxia is just Chinese mythic fantasy... right? If Exalted is a mythic fantasy RPG, and it can't do Wuxia, then Exalted is failing at its core goal.<br /> <br /> When I say things like bring the game closer to its Wuxia roots... that means focusing more on the mythic fantasy and less on things like modern Kung Fu Action films, or Shonen Martial Arts Tournament anime.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That's the game. </div> </div> </div>Citation needed.<br /> <br /> When is Exalted defined as a game where figuring out the best synergies and combos is a core aspect of what the game is meant to do?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don't want a system built around me having to take Water Dragon Charms to make my Tiger Stylist work. If I'm playing a Tiger Stylist, I want Tiger Style to be a whole and complete Martial Art that gives me a distinct fighting style. </div> </div> </div>Awesome. I'm not saying this should ever stop being the case. Let me express what I've been thinking about what this would actually look like to be more clear: <br /> <br /> Martial Arts Styles would work more like Evocations, but with Forms being the start of them and acting as the &quot;Artifact&quot; you need to be wielding to gain most or all of a style's benefits.<br /> <br /> Swapping Forms would be easier.<br /> <br /> The ability to combine styles would come at higher levels of mastery and possibly greater investment, rather than being the low level default.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don't want the Devs telling me how to make my character. I want them to give me the tools I need to make the character I want to make. </div> </div> </div>There's a hell of an excluded middle between &quot;The game has things that people will only learn through system mastery even though the devs could have just said it,&quot; and, &quot;the devs are telling you how to make your character.&quot;<br /> <br /> I want to have the tools I need to make the character I want to make. I consider the instruction manual on how the tools work to be an essential tool itself.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-07T20:53:20-07:00","id":1412530,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1411253-martial-arts-merit-cost?p=1411915#post1411915\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then mortals are a point of consideration here.</div> </div> </div> </div>They really aren\u2019t. Never have been, never will be. That there\u2019s a single sidebar of lip service to the fact a few people want to play one anyway doesn\u2019t change that, it emphasizes it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-07T21:48:30-07:00","id":1412540,"title":"","content":"&quot;The book includes rules for playing mortals therefore mortals aren't a consideration in the rules,&quot; is illogical nonsense.<br /> <br /> The &quot;never have been,&quot; part is particularly galling considering 2e's Scroll of the Monk and Scroll of Heroes. 3e's choice to get rid of Enlightened Mortals is something I think was the right move, but as sorcery ended up needing mortal sorcerer rules so they can access it without Essence or Charms (so that actually means two side-bars in Core alone...), 3e needed something to back up the setting still being steeped in mortal martial artists.<br /> <br /> Here's a simple way to analyze this:<br /> <br /> 1) Mortal play is not the default mode of play.<br /> <br /> 2) Mortal play is something some people still do.<br /> <br /> 3) The rules support mortal play.<br /> <br /> 4) Anything that improves mortal play without negatively impacting playing Exalts is a net positive for the game; even if Exalt should get the default focus.<br /> <br /> 5) Gatekeeping around mortal play is a net negative for the fandom.<br /> <br /> So... all of the &quot;mortals don't count&quot; crap is just that: crap. It doesn't make the game better, and it doesn't make the fandom feel as welcoming aspossible.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-08T00:01:07-07:00","id":1412547,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1411253-martial-arts-merit-cost?p=1412484#post1412484\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except... this whole thread is about how that's not exactly the case because Exalted puts martial arts in a weird place mechanically. Even at a minimum the 1 Ability dot and 4 Merit dot tax that the kung fu master has to deal with that the firewand specialist can just skill by going Archery makes this less true than it should be.</div> </div> </div> </div>That fact is more than compensated for by the breath of weapons the Martial Artist can use, the fact that they never need to Ready unarmed attacks, MA based Parry, the vast number of Martial Arts Charms available (including Righteous Devil Style), MA compatible Evocations, the fact that the Martial Artist can buy their combat Charms with Solar XP, and the fact that party balance is not a default position in Exalted (or Wuxia).<br /> <br /> Despite the 5 dot tax and buying each Martial Art separately, a Martial Artist PC is still incredibly strong mechanically.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1411253-martial-arts-merit-cost?p=1412540#post1412540\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So... all of the &quot;mortals don't count&quot; crap is just that: crap. It doesn't make the game better, and it doesn't make the fandom feel as welcoming aspossible.</div> </div> </div> </div>Your plucky group of mortals is never going to Craft Artifacts, learn Charms or defeat Octavian in combat.<br /> <br /> You are going to have to Orichalcum Rule Exalted to play mortal games. Removing the Merit cost for Mortal Martial Artists falls well within the purview of the OR. The Exalted ruleset provides for the fact that it doesn't provide for everything.<br /> <br /> Complaining on the Onyx Path forums doesn't change the published text written in the book. I'd encourage you to accept the proposed &quot;houserule&quot; of dropping the merit for mortals. If you want to talk about mortal martial artists, why not make a thread specifically about that? Because OP was asking about the impact of dropping the Merit for the Exalted, and that's what we're discussing in this thread. I'm sorry if it comes across as gatekeeping. Play the game you want to play.<br /> <br /> But the idea on the table is a free charm with merit purchase and waived cost for mortals. Do you have any actual input on the idea we're discussing? Or an alternate proposal to make?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 09-08-2020, 03:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-08T01:47:38-07:00","id":1412550,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1411253-martial-arts-merit-cost?p=1412547#post1412547\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That fact is more than compensated for by the breath of weapons the Martial Artist can use, the fact that they never need to Ready unarmed attacks, MA based Parry, the vast number of Martial Arts Charms available (including Righteous Devil Style), MA compatible Evocations, the fact that the Martial Artist can buy their combat Charms with Solar XP, and the fact that party balance is not a default position in Exalted (or Wuxia).</div> </div> </div> </div>The breadth of weapons you get from just buying Archery, Brawl, Melee, and Thrown separately is going to vastly out strip the breadth you're going to get from any four MA Styles, and doesn't have the Merit to account for.<br /> <br /> Evocations are a slim edge to native Charms: they're equally beneficial to either directly, but you have a free choice of Artifact armors to expand your Evocation options, and your Evocations aren't being bought with the same XP you'd be using to buy MA Charms.<br /> <br /> Etc.<br /> <br /> It's also fairly ridiculous to appeal to Exalted no caring about party balance when you're saying that the strength of the game is making if fun to play characters with different approaches to fighting. If you're going to make kung fu guy and firewand guy equally fun to play, one shouldn't be default better than the other (aka party balance should matter).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Despite the 5 dot tax and buying each Martial Art separately, a Martial Artist PC is still incredibly strong mechanically. </div> </div> </div>That &quot;despite&quot; is doing a lot of lifting here. MA PCs (well Solar ones... DBs dealing losing out on Mastery and dealing with Terrestrial get less bang for the same buck) aren't weak, but they're still putting in more resources and not coming out at leave even.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Your plucky group of mortals is never going to Craft Artifacts, learn Charms or defeat Octavian in combat. </div> </div> </div>Well, they can craft Artifacts (mortal sorcerers qualify), even if their chance of making high powered ones are low... but that's also not such a big deal since they can't do much with high level Artifacts anyway.<br /> <br /> And... so what? Terrestrials aren't going to be able to take on the same things as Solars even with the flatter power curve in 3e. Exalted was designed as a tiered game with different things to do at different levels of power.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You are going to have to Orichalcum Rule Exalted to play mortal games. </div> </div> </div>Not you're not. You probably should at for the MA Merit, but in general the rest of the rules that apply to mortals work just fine as is (or at least the problems in them are just as much there for mortals as Exalts)..<br /> <br /> And... you know, I suggested house ruling the MA Merit at the beginning of all this to make it a scaled Merit with it only costing 1 dot for mortal level skill. I don't need you to continue to post like I need to be reminded of things I've already said.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Complaining on the Onyx Path forums doesn't change the published text written in the book. </div> </div> </div>Tell that to LadyLens and Sith_Happens if you really care about this on general principle. They're complaining the mortals shouldn't be considered despite the published text written in the book.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'd encourage you to accept the proposed &quot;houserule&quot; of dropping the merit for mortals. </div> </div> </div>I posted my own house rules well before that. I don't need to &quot;be encouraged.&quot; Your posts <b>are not helpful</b> because they're raging condescension and hypocrisy, and it's far enough from the first time I've expressed this to take this as miscommunication or accident. Patronizing me because you think you're being smart by telling me shit I already know doesn't make your posts constructive no matter how nice you think you are in your head.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If you want to talk about mortal martial artists, why not make a thread specifically about that? </div> </div> </div>Because it's relevant to this thread.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Because OP was asking about the impact of dropping the Merit for the Exalted, and that's what we're discussing in this thread. </div> </div> </div>Bullshit:<br /> <br /> &quot;My new group just houserules that the Merit cost for MA makes no sense and that you can take it as an ability right out the gate. They want me to run a game for them and I'm hesitant as I'm new to the system to allow this. It seems that the cost of 4 (which is on par with Artifact 4 or Resources 4) is high enough to significantly affect the balance of the game if we were just to throw it away.<br /> <br /> Is there a good reason the MA merit is so expensive?&quot;<br /> <br /> The OP never specifically limits this to the Exalted and says to ignore mortals. The calls to ignore mortals only came after I pointed out certain fixes don't help with mortal martial arts.<br /> <br /> You're also in a piss poor position to talk about going off to start other threads. Why didn't you start another thread about Wuxia in Exalted which is far more divorced from the OP.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm sorry if it comes across as gatekeeping. Play the game you want to play. </div> </div> </div>Then you're not really sorry. If you don't want to gatekeep, don't help make this forum a place where &quot;mortal play isn't really Exalted,&quot; is an acceptable position.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But the idea on the table is a free charm with merit purchase and waived cost for mortals. Do you have any actual input on the idea we're discussing? Or an alternate proposal to make? </div> </div> </div>Are you fucking kidding me?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":617,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","user":"Heavy Arms","date":". 09-08-2020, 04:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-08T02:09:39-07:00","id":1412552,"title":"","content":"I'm not a mod, so I might be out of position, but I'd suggest to stop responding to people you feel offended by or eventually deal with them in private messages. I get that sometimes blood boil because people can be unnerving, but this is becoming more personal than necessary.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-08T02:11:13-07:00","id":1412553,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1411253-martial-arts-merit-cost?p=1412550#post1412550\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And... you know, I suggested house ruling the MA Merit at the beginning of all this to make it a scaled Merit with it only costing 1 dot for mortal level skill. I don't need you to continue to post like I need to be reminded of things I've already said.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I posted my own house rules well before that. <br /> <br /> Are you fucking kidding me?</div> </div> </div> </div>Would you like to discuss you ideas from page 1 further? You are the one who asked &quot;is there a better method besides the Merit tax?&quot;; I assumed the conversation had moved on but we can readdress those.<br /> <br /> MAs as specialities:<br /> <br /> I'd be inclined to go further and make MAs specialities in the other abilities (e.g. Brawl). Again, I think the RAW rules are fine, but if you're house-ruling stuff like Craft then bringing MA into line makes sense.<br /> <br /> Variable costs:<br /> <br /> It's an option. I'm not sure it addresses the fundamental issue of being a &quot;Merit Tax&quot;, especially for Solars and Immaculate Masters who basically gain nothing from the change. But it certainly addresses your concern for mortals.<br /> <br /> I think the free Charm/waiving the cost for mortals solution is probably more elegant.<br /> <br /> ****<br /> <br /> I think the 4 dot merit is fine. Most combatants in Creation are probably using Brawl. I can see Thrown and Melee being the next most popular with Archery dominating certain areas in Creation but not being widespread. I don't see armies of Martial Artists sweeping the land, and so using a 4 dot Merit for rarity is probably fine.<br /> <br /> But if you want to house-rule it, I don't think anything breaks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 09-08-2020, 05:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-08T03:42:32-07:00","id":1412559,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>This got a bit personal, could we dial it back and maybe consider if its worth posting if you feel baited? It's a discussion of the Martial Arts merit, it's not like we won't see a new iteration in a few months.</b></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-08T04:24:36-07:00","id":1412567,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1411253-martial-arts-merit-cost?p=1412553#post1412553\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the free Charm/waiving the cost for mortals solution is probably more elegant.</div> </div> </div> </div>It lacks elegance it the transition from mortal to Exalt; even just as a matter of background.<br /> <br /> Regardless of whether you're playing a pre-Exaltation game, or this is backstory that you feel is important enough to put dots down:<br /> <br /> You're playing a character that was an IO monk and as since left the Order while still mortal. You have, [Element] Dragon Style 1 because that's a requirement for monks to know, but haven't invested in MA beyond that. As a mortal, it's just one 1 Ability dot for some background flavor. OK.<br /> <br /> Then you Exalt as a Solar. What happens? Do you have to buy the Merit because you're an Exalt now? Even if you have no intention of increasing your MA let alone trying to find a sifu for one of the Dragon Styles? Do you have to raise your MA rating (none of the Dragon Styles have a Charm with a prerequisite below MA 2) so you can qualify for a free Charm in a Style you're not going to use?<br /> <br /> While the free Charm wasn't part of it, this is precisely where my variable cost MA Merit option came from: whether a minimal cost for mortals, or a minimal cost for some flavor to an Exalt, it's a smooth transition for more organically built characters.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don't see armies of Martial Artists sweeping the land, and so using a 4 dot Merit for rarity is probably fine. </div> </div> </div>As cited above, mortals training in Martial Arts Abilities is not rare according to the setting. Having the Merit for the sake of rarity makes no sense.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-08T15:39:37-07:00","id":1412646,"title":"","content":"So hypothetical alternative: Anyone can be trained in Style Ability dots, but you need the Supernatural Martial Artist merit before you can buy your first MA Charm.<br /> <br /> Better?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-08T16:26:45-07:00","id":1412652,"title":"","content":"Generally, though it calls into question why this is a Merit. It seems like it would be better just take the idea of initiation Charms from 2e and just have a universal starting MA Charm with some minor variations mostly for flavor for different ways of having come into supernatural MA. The Charm actually doing something gets rid of the &quot;tax&quot; issue, and you don't even have to worry about what Styles your character is going to focus on if that's something you intended to develop in-play.<br /> <br /> Eating up a Charm slot is a big deal (to most people probably a bigger deal than Merit dots) as far as gating goes. Bonus points its the same price for a 4 point Merit and a favored Charm. It's a relatively small savings fir you were buying it with XP. Though it raises the issue of if you can buy it with Solar XP or not.<br /> <br /> The idea of giving a free Charm with the Merit is OK, but most of the value of the Merit is then the Charm you get.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-08T21:18:27-07:00","id":1412678,"title":"","content":"I actually really like the initiation charm idea, it helps create a difference between MA and other forms of combat while not just sucking for the player.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9124-satoshi","name":"satoshi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"282"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-08T21:23:09-07:00","id":1412680,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blackwell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1411253-martial-arts-merit-cost?p=1412646#post1412646\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So hypothetical alternative: Anyone can be trained in Style Ability dots, but you need the Supernatural Martial Artist merit before you can buy your first MA Charm.<br /> <br /> Better?</div> </div> </div> </div>if you want to push that further you can even allow Charms to be bought for Style Abilities as normal BUT<br /> <br /> - You can not spend [Exalted] xp on MA Charms<br /> - Different Style Abilities count as different abilities so you cannot combine Charms across styles<br /> <br /> that would eliminate most of the edge over other Charm options that the MA Merit investment is largely paying for. It would make the Merit unnecessary for players who want to dabble in one specific thematic style that fits their character, but a necessary investment for tactically optimized centrally Martial Artist characters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-08T22:52:26-07:00","id":1412688,"title":"","content":"I still have yet to see what actual value the Merit brings. There's really nothing special in MA that requires a tax to balance out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-09T04:25:07-07:00","id":1412703,"title":"","content":"The value has been explained, even if you don't agree with the original devs on how much that value is really worth. The playtests showing MA was too cheap is a &quot;real&quot; problem, not a hypothetical one... the whole point of playtests is to find problems and address them. Disagree with the value the RAW rate that as all you want, but saying there's been not case made for there being some sort of gate isn't accurate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-09T06:37:33-07:00","id":1412711,"title":"","content":"I agree that there should be some gate, though I also agree that the RAW setup isn't really my favorite. I personally am fond of both &quot;just reduce the cost&quot; and &quot;full normal cost but you get a free MA Charm with it&quot;; neither are perfect but they've worked pleasantly for my purposes and that's been good enough on my end.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8026-beans","name":"Beans","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8026_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"472"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-09T16:40:15-07:00","id":1412768,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1411253-martial-arts-merit-cost?p=1412703#post1412703\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The value has been explained, even if you don't agree with the original devs on how much that value is really worth. The playtests showing MA was too cheap is a &quot;real&quot; problem, not a hypothetical one... the whole point of playtests is to find problems and address them. Disagree with the value the RAW rate that as all you want, but saying there's been not case made for there being some sort of gate isn't accurate.</div> </div> </div> </div>Going back to Page 1:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kelly Pedersen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1411253-martial-arts-merit-cost?p=1411257#post1411257\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>I wasn't part of the playtes</b>t for Ex3, <b>but I'm told that what happened</b>, when there <i>wasn't</i> a Martial Artist merit, everybody basically bought martial arts styles. It's basically combat charms that you can spend Solar XP on, which makes it <i>extremely</i> competitive, if not purely better, than the native Solar combat Abilities, if there's no extra buy-in via the merit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Bold emphasis mine. So far these playtest reports are all &quot;Well I wasn't there but...&quot; and &quot;Solar XP&quot;. Meanwhile, in this thread, those of us who dropped the merit entirely (myself included) haven't noticed a change in power levels, which is Actual Play Experience. Does anyone have a link to the actual playtesters talking about this?<br /> <br /> I don't agree that the argument &quot;well you can dip into many styles&quot; is worth anything because there are no MA 1 dot charms, and only one or two 2 dot charms in each Style, so you already have to run a build like Snake 2 /Tiger 3 /Ebon Shadow 2 to get the low hanging fruit... which you could have just done with Athletics or Stealth. Form Charms are probably the strongest MA exclusive you get and yet it hasn't really been brought up that much (they also require MA 4 across the board***). Even then, aside from SIngle Point, most form charms are some version &quot;extra damage&quot; or &quot;extra defense&quot;. Even still, So What? Who Cares? If you <b>aren't</b> a Dawn, than the number of available charms for your precious Solar XP is <b><i>severely</i></b> gated behind your Essence. If you <b>are</b> a Dawn, then going multi-MA is a style choice, because the standard Brawl Grappler or Melee Swordsman is a much stronger build anyway. And this circles around to my post on page 1: If Solar XP was such a problem <i>just don't let Solar XP be used on MA Charms</i>.<br /> <br /> At the risk of besmirching the hard work of the Ex3 team, I'm sorry to say this but, I honestly don't think the devs really had a good handle on balance in the first place and we should be taking their opinions with a grain of salt. Remember <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1015932-do-heavy-melee-weapons-kind-of-suck\">this thread on heavy weapons</a>? The many threads about how poor the Naval Combat system is? The Skill that shall not be named? So forgive me if I don't put a lot of weight into Developer Playtest Experience, let alone <i>Secondhand</i> Developer Playtest Experience.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\"><i>***Righteous Devil alone takes 3, which seems like an accident</i></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":8830,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","user":"Sorcerous Overlord","date":". 09-09-2020, 07:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-09T17:06:57-07:00","id":1412769,"title":"","content":"OK. Seriously. So what?<br /> <br /> The vast majority of the posters in the thread seem to agree the Merit is bad. Whether they think gating is completely unnecessary, or they think some gating is appropriate, the clear majority say a Merit tax was the wrong way to do it.<br /> <br /> What does debating the validity of reports about the playtest do? What does trying to assert one group's play experience as more important than different group's play experience? It's entirely possible different groups have different experiences with the same mechanics.<br /> <br /> Your position has been stated. You don't have to agree with people that think there should be some gating to help come up with a better gate than the original devs did. Where are you trying to go with this then?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-09T17:46:54-07:00","id":1412775,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1411253-martial-arts-merit-cost?p=1412688#post1412688\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I still have yet to see what actual value the Merit brings. There's really nothing special in MA that requires a tax to balance out.</div> </div> </div> </div>1) you can spend Solar/Dragon/etc xp on it<br /> <br /> 2) you can combine charms across styles for a degree of tactical syncronicity that a normal Ability Charm set does not facilitate<br /> <br /> Note that as I said before your post though, BOTH OF THESE ADVANTAGES ARE EASY TO REMOVE for a MA dabbler or single-style specialist who isn\u2019t taking advantage of them and doesn\u2019t want to pay the entry fee.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-09T19:22:02-07:00","id":1412782,"title":"","content":"It basically lets you start buying evocations for your hands, as I think somebody brought up in this thread earlier.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-09T19:53:44-07:00","id":1412784,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1411253-martial-arts-merit-cost?p=1412769#post1412769\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">OK. Seriously. So what?<br /> <br /> The vast majority of the posters in the thread seem to agree the Merit is bad. Whether they think gating is completely unnecessary, or they think some gating is appropriate, the clear majority say a Merit tax was the wrong way to do it.<br /> <br /> <b>(1)What does debating the validity of reports about the playtest do? (2)What does trying to assert one group's play experience as more important than different group's play experience? (3)It's entirely possible different groups have different experiences with the same mechanics.</b><br /> <br /> Your position has been stated. You don't have to agree with people that think there should be some gating to help come up with a better gate than the original devs did. <b>(4)</b><b>Where are you trying to go with this then?</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Numbers are mine. let's address those in order.<br /> <br /> 1) The topic of this thread is about a merit tax, which is justified<b> entirely </b>on playtest results none of us have ever seen or had a firsthand account of.<br /> 2) This justification doesn't match the experience of current players.<br /> 3) A meaningless addition, that maxim holds true of almost every system of every rpg.<br /> 4) Explaining my rationale to your assertation that MA comboing was a &quot;real&quot; problem.<br /> <br /> I feel that further discussion isn't going to be productive since, if I have this right, your stance is that since my opinion is stated and therefore I don't need to discuss it further. If that's not your position I apologize, but regardless, I don't think this thread is gonna go anywhere. As you said, most of us stand in strong opposition to the Martial Arts Merit.<br /> <br /> This is also getting a little heated, so I'd just like to take a step back and thank everyone who contributed so far. <br /> Edit: I just had to add when i saw this: <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1411253-martial-arts-merit-cost?p=1412782#post1412782\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It basically lets you start buying evocations for your hands, as I think somebody brought up in this thread earlier.</div> </div> </div> </div>best Sentence I've read all day. I'd be a lot more accepting of the Martial Arts merit if it made your hands/legs whatever into artifact damage form weapons","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":8830,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","user":"Sorcerous Overlord","date":". 09-09-2020, 10:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-09T20:02:31-07:00","id":1412786,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1411253-martial-arts-merit-cost?p=1412784#post1412784\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd be a lot more accepting of the Martial Arts merit if it made your hands/legs whatever into artifact damage form weapons</div> </div> </div> </div>That's...maybe a bit too far. They'd be artifact weapons that not only never give away that you're armed, but also don't let everyone know you're Exalted/Anathema, don't take attunement motes, and can't be taken from you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-09T20:06:48-07:00","id":1412787,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1411253-martial-arts-merit-cost?p=1412786#post1412786\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's...maybe a bit too far. They'd be artifact weapons that not only never give away that you're armed, but also don't let everyone know you're Exalted/Anathema, don't take attunement motes, and can't be taken from you.</div> </div> </div> </div>Those are good points. Mostly for attunement and social stealth. I don't think I've ever seen a player disarmed in game, and glove weapons or shoes are usually immune to that. Maybe they light up when you channel your Snake Style essence into them &quot;Green Hand of the Serpent&quot; style. But i'm just spitballing here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-09T20:21:13-07:00","id":1412790,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1411253-martial-arts-merit-cost?p=1412787#post1412787\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think I've ever seen a player disarmed in game, and glove weapons or shoes are usually immune to that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have disarmed a player once or twice, but I may also be an outlier. I've basically never used cover but I'm trying to in the future and other people might use it all the time. The real place I see people being disarmed is when they're being forcibly disarmed, or disarmed by social pressure or tradition, to go to an event.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1411253-martial-arts-merit-cost?p=1412787#post1412787\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe they light up when you channel your Snake Style essence into them &quot;Green Hand of the Serpent&quot; style. But i'm just spitballing here.</div> </div> </div> </div>That could work. If you had to attune them and they covered your limbs in energy, but couldn't be taken away that might be a good kind of attunement bonus for an artifact 4 weapon. Imagine them like artifact shortswords who's attunement bonus is to vanish to Elsewhere until recalled. Basically Call the Blade for free.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-09T22:19:25-07:00","id":1412798,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think I've ever seen a player disarmed in game\u2026</div> </div> </div> </div>It made for a pretty serious bit of tension in my West game when the Eclipse got disarmed, as his dice pool for unarmed was drastically lower.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-09T22:50:28-07:00","id":1412803,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1411253-martial-arts-merit-cost?p=1412798#post1412798\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It made for a pretty serious bit of tension in my West game when the Eclipse got disarmed, as his dice pool for unarmed was drastically lower.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm a big fan of this. It's also just a good thing to think about with a fighting character in general. You get 28 ability dots at chargen. If somebody takes away your sword and you drop from 14+10 dice of attack and Parry 7+5 to 9 dice of attack with parry 3, and no charms, that could be bad. Something that was trivial before instantly becomes deadly. <br /> <br /> If you're a fighter to your core, think really hard before you dump Archery, Thrown, Brawl, and Dodge to zero. It could bite you in the butt later and make you look foolish, and there's a decent chance it doesn't even make sense for your character.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-10T00:29:49-07:00","id":1412812,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1411253-martial-arts-merit-cost?p=1412803#post1412803\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm a big fan of this. It's also just a good thing to think about with a fighting character in general. You get 28 ability dots at chargen. If somebody takes away your sword and you drop from 14+10 dice of attack and Parry 7+5 to 9 dice of attack with parry 3, and no charms, that could be bad. Something that was trivial before instantly becomes deadly. <br /> <br /> If you're a fighter to your core, think really hard before you dump Archery, Thrown, Brawl, and Dodge to zero. It could bite you in the butt later and make you look foolish, and there's a decent chance it doesn't even make sense for your character.</div> </div> </div> </div>It wasn\u2019t <i>quite</i> that bad - he had thankfully taken my advice and dipped into Brawl enough to get the amazing Thunderclap Rush Attack.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-10T03:23:29-07:00","id":1412826,"title":"","content":"One of my favorite moments in a rather long exalted game was when a party of 700+ XP Solars accepted a challenge from a group of Lunars to try and fight a pack of normal wolves without their weapons. The party assumed they would be fine but quickly realized that despite all their xp, none of those present that session had a single dot in brawl or MA. A pack of 6 completely normal wolves almost wrecked 4 high-xp solars, it was hilarious.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9124-satoshi","name":"satoshi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"282"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-10T04:49:56-07:00","id":1412832,"title":"","content":"I like the idea that MA gives you access to virtually &quot;artifacts weapons&quot;, with maybe an attisement cost of some sort. It's fun, I think I'll use it in my next game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-10T05:07:50-07:00","id":1412834,"title":"","content":"If that\u2019s what you want, you should just take Silver-Voiced Nightingale Style. Its initial charm upgrades your voice into an effective artifact weapon if you\u2019re a Solar.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-10T05:30:28-07:00","id":1412835,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1411253-martial-arts-merit-cost?p=1412834#post1412834\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If that\u2019s what you want, you should just take Silver-Voiced Nightingale Style. Its initial charm upgrades your voice into an effective artifact weapon if you\u2019re a Solar.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know but I didn't think of extending it to other Martial Arts. It's a way to make the 4 dot merit cost interesting, by just including it as a standard feature.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-10T05:34:51-07:00","id":1412837,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1411253-martial-arts-merit-cost?p=1412835#post1412835\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I know but I didn't think of extending it to other Martial Arts. It's a way to make the 4 dot merit cost interesting, by just including it as a standard feature.</div> </div> </div> </div>This was also done once in 2.5e with Cobra Style. The entry Charm was Cobra Fang Technique (or similar name), a Permanent that gave you a new artifact-quality unarmed &quot;weapon&quot; that counted as a Form weapon for Cobra Style but, notably, not other Styles.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-10T05:41:06-07:00","id":1412839,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blackwell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1411253-martial-arts-merit-cost?p=1412837#post1412837\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This was also done once in 2.5e with Cobra Style. The entry Charm was Cobra Fang Technique (or similar name), a Permanent that gave you a new artifact-quality unarmed &amp;quot;weapon&amp;quot; that counted as a Form weapon for Cobra Style but, notably, not other Styles.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well I think it's something I'm willing to accept to extend to other MA it seems fun","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-10T06:10:17-07:00","id":1412842,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1411253-martial-arts-merit-cost?p=1412839#post1412839\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well I think it's something I'm willing to accept to extend to other MA it seems fun</div> </div> </div> </div>If it's useful, I dug this out of my archive:<br /> <br /> <b>Showing the Cobra\u2019s Fangs</b><br /> Cost: \u2014; Mins: Martial Arts 2, Essence 2; <br /> Type: Permanent<br /> Keywords: None<br /> Duration: Permanent<br /> Prerequisite Charms: None <br /> The Cobra stylist forms his hands into the famous fangs for which this style is known. Bending and poising his fingers into perfect receptacles for his killing Essence, his \u201chand fang\u201d strike gains the following stats: Speed 5, Accuracy +3, Damage +5L, Defense +2, Rate 1, Tags: N. A character using this attack adds one automatic success to all Martial Arts attacks which seek to Poison the target. The Cobra\u2019s Fangs share Rate with the martial artist\u2019s punch attack; so, since a punch is Rate 3, the character could punch twice and fang strike once in a single flurry. The Cobra\u2019s Fangs are considered an unarmed attack for the purpose of Cobra style Charms, or for any Martial Arts Charm with the Poison Keyword, but are not compatible with any other Charms of any other style.<br /> When the character has learned the Charm Marked by Eternity, his fangs are further enhanced: they now do 8L Damage, have a Defense of +3, and add two automatic successes to Poison-inflicting Martial Arts attacks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-10T06:26:11-07:00","id":1412843,"title":"","content":"Hmmm. I don't think I would implement this as a Charm, but I'm not sure yet. The final effect I would like would probably be these : Every Martial Artist (so, that payed 4 dots of Merit) is somehow able to treat his martial weapon he uses with the Martial Weapon skills and Charms as having Artefacts stats, with the same constraint as those (attunement cost, for example) to avoid someone taking Martial Arts solely to gain the effects of Artifacts with pure mechanical advantages, for example. I'm not sure yet on some limits I would add or other specificities but it seems to be a nice catch to me for paying the 4 dot merit Martial Arts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-10T23:14:56-07:00","id":1412964,"title":"","content":"You can hardly compare an artifact to an MA style.<br /> <br /> It's true that they're usually the same power as an artifact 4, but the issue is that when I get an artifact I usually have a suite of base competency charms in my natural charmset. Anything the artifact doesn't cover will be covered by my native charms.<br /> <br /> MA forces you to either live with the (sometimes fairly huge) gaps in your charmset or forces you to buy up an entirely new combat ability. This is often rare for native sets, which give your character the ability to do almost anything and typically I don't need to repurchase another whole ability. I don't need to do that for an evocation.<br /> <br /> This was so problematic I had to make homebrew in order to make it tolerable (Expanded Lotus).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Read my shit at my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/271207-sandact6-homebrew-topic\" target=\"_blank\">homebrew</a> topic, 2.5e and 3e material!<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1263020-alchemicals-2-0-3e-conversion-charm-design-request\" target=\"_blank\">Play Alchemical's in 3e now</a>, you're welcome.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1183-sandact6","name":"Sandact6","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1183_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-11T00:13:05-07:00","id":1412968,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>satoshi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1411253-martial-arts-merit-cost?p=1412826#post1412826\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of my favorite moments in a rather long exalted game was when a party of 700+ XP Solars accepted a challenge from a group of Lunars to try and fight a pack of normal wolves without their weapons. The party assumed they would be fine but quickly realized that despite all their xp, none of those present that session had a single dot in brawl or MA. A pack of 6 completely normal wolves almost wrecked 4 high-xp solars, it was hilarious.</div> </div> </div> </div>That sound you hear is Sir Lancelot laughing the hardest.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-11T00:20:54-07:00","id":1412969,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sandact6</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1411253-martial-arts-merit-cost?p=1412964#post1412964\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can hardly compare an artifact to an MA style.<br /> <br /> It's true that they're usually the same power as an artifact 4, but the issue is that when I get an artifact I usually have a suite of base competency charms in my natural charmset. Anything the artifact doesn't cover will be covered by my native charms.<br /> <br /> MA forces you to either live with the (sometimes fairly huge) gaps in your charmset or forces you to buy up an entirely new combat ability. This is often rare for native sets, which give your character the ability to do almost anything and typically I don't need to repurchase another whole ability. I don't need to do that for an evocation.<br /> <br /> This was so problematic I had to make homebrew in order to make it tolerable (Expanded Lotus).</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm unsure of your comparison. If one of my player took an artifact 3 designed for fight with a Charmtree of around 10 Charms that do a specific related to the artifact, it'd be just like having a MA with some different conditions at the limit (not being disarmed, 1 merit point cost difference, etc ...). Even Artifacts 4 and 5 have potentially a lot more of Evocations but it's only if you take the hassle of designing them, if you don't because you just want the cool artifact to do what's written on it it's basically a MA.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-11T06:44:29-07:00","id":1413004,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1411253-martial-arts-merit-cost?p=1412969#post1412969\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm unsure of your comparison. If one of my player took an artifact 3 designed for fight with a Charmtree of around 10 Charms that do a specific related to the artifact, it'd be just like having a MA with some different conditions at the limit (not being disarmed, 1 merit point cost difference, etc ...). Even Artifacts 4 and 5 have potentially a lot more of Evocations but it's only if you take the hassle of designing them, if you don't because you just want the cool artifact to do what's written on it it's basically a MA.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thing is an artifact is going to be fundamentally different first of all. Almost all artifacts are written with the assumption that you'll have your native charms to bolster them. I'm not saying that an artifact cannot have offensive or defense stuff, but they're made with the assumption of &quot;Oh yea, the dude taking this will have an offense/defense suite that will allow them to expand past any holes the evocation suite has.&quot;<br /> <br /> MA's cannot assume this. MA's assume you're either taking dodge or using their native parry charms (which then need to be made into the MA). MA's contain a lot more generic workhorse charms than an evocation suite, which assumes you already have that by default. Usually any workhorse charms an evocation set has are effects that typically link up to later charms or match the theme of the artifact.<br /> <br /> That's my point. I think making the MA = Evocations thing is a very design trap to fall into myself. They're similar, but pretty different.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Read my shit at my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/271207-sandact6-homebrew-topic\" target=\"_blank\">homebrew</a> topic, 2.5e and 3e material!<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1263020-alchemicals-2-0-3e-conversion-charm-design-request\" target=\"_blank\">Play Alchemical's in 3e now</a>, you're welcome.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1183-sandact6","name":"Sandact6","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1183_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-11T07:20:25-07:00","id":1413009,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sandact6</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1411253-martial-arts-merit-cost?p=1413004#post1413004\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thing is an artifact is going to be fundamentally different first of all. Almost all artifacts are written with the assumption that you'll have your native charms to bolster them. I'm not saying that an artifact cannot have offensive or defense stuff, but they're made with the assumption of &quot;Oh yea, the dude taking this will have an offense/defense suite that will allow them to expand past any holes the evocation suite has.&quot;<br /> <br /> MA's cannot assume this. MA's assume you're either taking dodge or using their native parry charms (which then need to be made into the MA). MA's contain a lot more generic workhorse charms than an evocation suite, which assumes you already have that by default. Usually any workhorse charms an evocation set has are effects that typically link up to later charms or match the theme of the artifact.<br /> <br /> That's my point. I think making the MA = Evocations thing is a very design trap to fall into myself. They're similar, but pretty different.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes okay I see your point. I think for my games I'd go along with it because I'm not trying to make MA into Artefacts, but rather to give something interesting to MA that compel them a bit more to go into it without losing too much points (4 is a lot for solely accessing the Charms). I think I'd like to see a bit more characters using some new Charms and have really personalized way of fighting instead of hearing the eternal &quot;I use Perfect Strike&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-11T07:25:55-07:00","id":1413012,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sandact6</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1411253-martial-arts-merit-cost?p=1412964#post1412964\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">MA forces you to either live with the (sometimes fairly huge) gaps in your charmset or forces you to buy up an entirely new combat ability. This is often rare for native sets, which give your character the ability to do almost anything and typically I don't need to repurchase another whole ability.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. There's a reason why thus far only Lunars have parity between the xp costs for Evocations and Martial Arts charms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-11T10:07:13-07:00","id":1413052,"title":"","content":"Is anyone hoping for any particular solutions in Exalted: Essence?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-11T10:57:00-07:00","id":1413059,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1411253-martial-arts-merit-cost?p=1413052#post1413052\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is anyone hoping for any particular solutions in Exalted: Essence?</div> </div> </div> </div>In Essence Martial Arts Charms <i>are</i> Close Combat/Ranged Combat Charms, so there should be no need to gate them behind a merit. At worst I could see like a 1 dot cost per MA just so people don't dip into them nilly-willy, but I don't expect a whopping 4 dot gate (or whatever the equivalent of merit dots will be in Essence).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-11T14:34:17-07:00","id":1413107,"title":"","content":"I'm hoping Essence does approach MA in a different way in general.<br /> <br /> I haven't kept up on the news, so I don't know how much detail MA has gotten in the previews.<br /> <br /> What I'd hope is that MA (as the whole project's goal is to reduce things and make them more manageable), if it is going to remain its own thing, would be reduced to single Form Charms rather than distinct combat Charm trees; or at least something similar.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-11T16:23:17-07:00","id":1413126,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1411253-martial-arts-merit-cost?p=1413107#post1413107\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm hoping Essence does approach MA in a different way in general.<br /> <br /> I haven't kept up on the news, so I don't know how much detail MA has gotten in the previews.<br /> <br /> What I'd hope is that MA (as the whole project's goal is to reduce things and make them more manageable), if it is going to remain its own thing, would be reduced to single Form Charms rather than distinct combat Charm trees; or at least something similar.</div> </div> </div> </div>With all Close Combat Charms and Ranged Combat Charms being universal, it seems like a great opportunity to cut out a lot of what Exalted has treated as &quot;Martial Arts&quot;.<br /> <br /> Have a short Ranged Combat Charm tree for projectiles in general, a separate short tree specifically for small throwing blades, another for larger projectiles like javelins, a tree for firewands that easily encompasses everything Righteous Devil Style could offer (including a Form Charm that forbids armor)...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-11T18:21:49-07:00","id":1413144,"title":"","content":"I highly doubt we'll see Essence go into specific Charms for individual classes of weapons that narrow. We don't have basic Charms now that care about throwing knives vs. javelins.<br /> <br /> I would much rather see page count on something like the idea of MA-as-single-Form-Charms that make you really good with a small selection of weapons (esp. with broader Abilities) and some boosts with cross-ability appeal. One Righteous Devil Form Charm is, to me, valuable. 2-3 firewarnd specific universal Charms are less so; at least from what I understand of Essence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-11T20:45:25-07:00","id":1413154,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1411253-martial-arts-merit-cost?p=1413144#post1413144\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I highly doubt we'll see Essence go into specific Charms for individual classes of weapons that narrow. We don't have basic Charms now that care about throwing knives vs. javelins.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's because basic Charms and Martial Arts Charms are already separate.<br /> <br /> But see, when there's no Thrown or Archery or Righteous Devil Martial Arts or Night Breeze Martial Arts or Air Dragon Martial Arts, just a single &quot;Ranged Combat&quot; Ability, then you can already anticipate Charm trees for archery separate from throwing weapons, and potentially a set of Charms for chakram (Air Dragon) separate from those for throwing knives (Night Breeze).<br /> <br /> Though it's entirely possible that the Charms simply won't have that much granularity, and weapons will contain all of their unique traits within themselves through a Tag system like vanilla Third Edition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-11T21:29:48-07:00","id":1413158,"title":"","content":"Oh, I think there will be &quot;archery&quot; and &quot;thrown&quot; Charms in Essence, but I think they're going to be capstones or offshoots of the core tree for ranged rather than full separate trees. I don't think we'll see many of them though, because there isn't as much of a need to give Archery and Thrown their own flavors in Essence. Instead of Thrown getting a lot more &quot;trick&quot; Charms to Archery's direct boosting, I don't think Essence has a good reason to worry about that.<br /> <br /> Which opens up space for MA.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}